      {
        "id": 24741,
        "name": "TheJayMann",
        "username": "TheJayMann",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/thejaymann/{size}/2261_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-01-29T10:01:16.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>So when I was counting Wraith cards, I was missing one card (specifically, Utility Belt, the same card awmiller claimed to be missing).  Today while setting up a game, I counted my Omnitron deck and found it was missing a card (all other decks were accounted for).  Specifically, it apeared I was missing Terraforming.  So, it appeared I was missing the last card of the hero cards and the last card of the villian cards, as well as missing the same exact cards awmiller was missing.  I also found said missing cards.  Turns out the cards were sticking to each other.  I’m guessing maybe the coating isnt drying all the way before they cut and stacked them at the printer.  Though, this would only likely affect people with a recently opened copy of the game.  Playing a game or two would generate enough stress on the cards to break any adhesion between the cards.</p>",
        "post_number": 28,
        "post_type": 1,
